; Puppeteer's "do not download a browser" setting used to live here as
; puppeteer_skip_chromium_download=true. npm has never known that key — it is
; read by puppeteer's own install script — and npm 9+ now reports it on every
; command as an unknown project/env config.
;
; It moved to puppeteer.config.cjs (skipDownload), which is where Puppeteer
; v19+ looks. Nothing about the browser workflow changed: this project depends
; on puppeteer-core, which never downloads anything, and src/utils/launchBrowser.ts
; resolves an installed Chrome/Edge — or @sparticuz/chromium — at runtime.
